// A table's field, or a plain list, may be a text of any length: the
// bytes are the program's own, and what is read is a view of them (a
// text without bytes where there is no such row), which a field takes a
// copy of like any other.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/tables_text.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.out
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/tables_text.ent 2>/dev/null | cmp - %t.out
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.out

// CHECK:      arrow: 94 bytes: Hits the foe in its reach that is furthest along the road, again and again, and that one only.
// CHECK-NEXT: cannon: 0 bytes: 
